# Risk surfaces: how much human and agent review attention a change to a path deserves.
# Read from the BASE branch by the pre-push review (skills-internal cross-model-review), so a PR
# cannot lower the tier of its own files. Format: `<tier> <glob>`, last match wins; a glob with no
# `/` matches at any depth. Defaults already make replication/ critical and security/ sensitive.
#
# critical  — correctness or durability of stored data, replication, cluster membership
# sensitive — authentication, authorization, keys and certificates, licensing, request filtering
# hot       — per-request or per-message paths where a regression is a performance incident
# ordinary  — overrides a broader line above it

critical  cloneNode/
critical  bin/repairDeleteEchoRuns.ts

sensitive cloneNode/jwtKeyClone.ts
sensitive cloneNode/sshKeyClone.ts
sensitive licensing/
sensitive waf/

# One tier per path: replication's per-message paths (frameWriter, replicationConnection) are hot
# too, but they also define the wire format, so they stay critical.
hot       waf/matcher.ts

ordinary  replication/logRedaction.ts
ordinary  replication/blobSendWarnThrottle.ts
ordinary  replication/subscribeDeferralForTest.ts
ordinary  replication/record-lock-*-runs/
